    notes: 'Tokyo select-shop and original-clothing business launched in Harajuku in February 1976 as American Life Shop BEAMS. Etsuzo Shitara financed the new apparel business; Osamu Shigematsu developed the store concept and ran the first shop, with Yo Shitara also participating in its establishment. Distinct from the parent packaging company’s 1953 origin and the operating company’s 1982 incorporation. This entry covers the broader fashion business, including its own menswear and womenswear labels; individual creative roles retain their line scopes. American casualwear, Ivy references and utility clothing are important threads. Stocking or collaborating with another brand does not establish designer employment there.',
