    notes: 'London eyewear label known for treating sunglasses as a central part of a fashion wardrobe. Oversized shapes, unusual geometry and vintage references sit alongside restrained optical frames, using materials including Japanese titanium, gold and Italian acetate. Founded by Linda Farrow in 1970, the brand paused production before its 2003 revival by her son Simon Jablon and Tracy Sedino.',
