    notes: 'Tokyo label of designer Tokihito Yoshida, rooted in British and American heritage outerwear, biker clothing and tailoring. Waxed-cotton and nylon jackets, refined workwear coats and practical details such as poacher pockets and removable hoods define the line. Menswear launched in 1997 and womenswear followed in 1998. Yoshida is best known outside Japan for the Barbour Beacon Heritage range he designed from 2009. Current activity is not confirmed.',
