    notes: 'Italian no-logo outerwear label built to last. Its name abbreviates "The Emperor’s New Clothes". Military-inspired parkas, field jackets and liners are made in Italy and garment-dyed, waxed or sealed so they wear in with use. The founding fabric is OJJ (Original Japanese Jersey), a dense nylon-polyester with an almost leather-like hand, alongside nylon gabardine and resin-coated linen. Former C.P. Company and Stone Island designers Alessandro Pungetti and Paul Harvey began with seven pieces; Harvey left after a few years. Some profiles date the founding to 2010; Pungetti dates it to 2012.',
