    notes: 'Spanish footwear brand known for chunky gothic, metal and biker boots with towering platform soles, flame-shaped metal hardware, buckles and chains, alongside western boots, platform trainers, leather jackets and accessories. Its lines are named Metal, Rock, Cyber, Casual, Biker and Western. The brand grew out of the Ortuño family’s shoemaking in Yecla, which dates to 1929; the official history dates New Rock itself to 1980 under Pedro Ortuño, while other accounts give 1978 for the family company. Its anatomically injected Comfort Plus sole is a signature technical feature.',
