    instagram: 'lucchese',
    logo: 'lucchese.webp',
    notes: 'Texas maker of handcrafted cowboy boots in exotic and calf leathers, built on a twisted-cone last with lemonwood pegs and known for elaborate stitchwork, including the State Boots collection begun in 1949. The range spans men’s and women’s western boots, ropers, leather goods, belts, shirts and western apparel. Sicilian brothers Salvatore and Joseph Lucchese opened the first shop near Fort Sam Houston in San Antonio in 1883, making boots for cavalry officers; Salvatore’s son Cosimo incorporated it as Lucchese Boot Company in 1929. Production moved to El Paso in 1986 and remains there, while the company is now headquartered in the Dallas Design District. Renamed Lucchese Bootmaker in 2012.',
