    instagram: 'jackvictorofficial',
    logo: 'jack_victor.webp',
    notes: 'Family-run Montreal maker of men’s tailored clothing: suits, sport coats, blazers, trousers and outerwear, plus shirts, knitwear and accessories. Its tailoring is still cut and sewn in Montreal, with classic proportions and a reputation for consistent fit. Founder Jack Victor, a Romanian immigrant, started out selling clothes door to door; in 1947 he became sole owner of the Royal Brand Clothing Company and renamed it Jack Victor & Sons. The McCord Stewart Museum traces his start to 1907; the company gives 1913.',
    sources: ['https://encyclomodeqc.musee-mccord-stewart.ca/en/entry/jack-victor/', 'https://www.jackvictor.com/pages/our-world', 'https://nuvomagazine.com/magazine/autumn-2022/jack-victors-remarkably-consistent-tailoring'],
