    notes: 'Menswear label bridging Italian tailoring and Chinese heritage, sometimes called “street tailoring”: reworked Mao and workwear jackets, wide trousers, padded outerwear and knits, with embroidery, crafts and folk motifs from across China. Often gender-neutral and shown on women too. Founded by two Chinese designers working between Milan and Shanghai; Woolmark Prize finalist in 2017 and the first Chinese label to stage a runway show at Pitti Uomo, in 2019. It now shows in Milan.',
