    notes: 'German fashion brand founded by Wolfgang Joop in Hamburg. It is known for polished menswear: suits (including modular suits), blazers, shirts, coats, leather jackets and knitwear. It also makes womenswear and the JOOP! Jeans line, first released in 1988 and revived in 2016 with its 1990s logo, plus bags, luggage and a home collection. The capital-letter logo with an exclamation mark and Joop\'s favourite flower, the cornflower, are its emblems. Its fragrances, from JOOP! Homme (1988) on, are made under licence. Joop sold most of the company in 1998 and left in 2001. Designed at the JOOP! Villa in Hamburg, its former atelier, since 2016; the operating company is in Kreuzlingen.',
